## Contract changes in the test file

- The stub `tsx` prints the value of `DOCTOR_GATE_TSX_STDOUT` on stdout, one line for each line of the value. The real CLI writes the verdict line to stdout.
- `reset_tsx` unsets `DOCTOR_GATE_TSX_MESSAGE` and `DOCTOR_GATE_TSX_STDOUT`. Each new case calls `reset_tsx` first.
- The three old cases `tsx_exit_1_gate_exits_0`, `architecture_line_shows_code`, and `no_write_in_root` print the whole verdict line on stderr. The last one also asserts the boundary clause for the code 1 run.
- The verdict literal of every new case is `architecture check: debt-change (files=12, findings=3, parseErrors=0)`.
- The pinned lines of FR-3 are asserted as whole lines. Every tool failure case asserts that the output holds no boundary gate line. Every boundary case asserts that the output holds no tool failure text.

## Harness notes

- Each case builds its own root under `/tmp` with `mktemp -d`, copies `measure/doctor.sh` into `<tmp>/measure/`, writes three stub guards into `<tmp>/tests/`, and writes the stub `tsx` into `<tmp>/node_modules/.bin/tsx`. The stub logs its argv in `<tmp>/tsx.log`.
- The `PATH` of every run is `<tmp>/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`. No real `pnpm` and no real `tsx` runs.
- The exit codes are asserted as integers. Each count carries a label.
- Part B reads the record through the `track_dir_resolve` helper, which prefers `measure/archive/<id>` over `measure/tracks/<id>`.
- Each case removes its own root. No fixture entered the repository. No production file changed.

## Sanity check of the test

A scratch copy of the test file and a scratch copy of `measure/doctor.sh` that holds the planned rule of task 3.0b make all 19 cases pass with `cases_total=19 cases_failed=0`. The scratch root sat outside the repository and was removed. The real `measure/doctor.sh` did not change.

The Red state is satisfiable. The four failing cases fail for the rule of F207 alone.

